WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.963
Here's what you'll be able to
do by the end of this module.

2
00:00:02.963 --> 00:00:06.035
You'll build a filtering
policy, a security profile,

3
00:00:06.035 --> 00:00:10.425
the link between them, and the
Conditional Access policy that assigns it.

4
00:00:10.425 --> 00:00:14.710
You'll explain why both the Microsoft
and internet profiles are enabled,

5
00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:16.638
and what Learn's limits leave out.

6
00:00:16.638 --> 00:00:20.875
You'll govern every bypass and
allow-list entry with an owner,

7
00:00:20.875 --> 00:00:22.400
a reason and an expiry.

8
00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:26.134
You'll choose the certificate
authority for T L S inspection,

9
00:00:26.134 --> 00:00:28.375
and deploy trust before activation.

10
00:00:28.375 --> 00:00:32.168
And you'll set the privacy boundary,
handle pinned applications,

11
00:00:32.168 --> 00:00:35.388
and read the T L S outcomes
against the one percent line.

12
00:00:35.388 --> 00:00:41.406
You need Module 2, Network and Transport,
chapter five, on Internet Access policy,

13
00:00:41.406 --> 00:00:47.150
and a skim of PKI and Certificates, chapter
four, for the dedicated issuing C A.

14
00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:50.380
The lab runs in a test
tenant, never production.
